1
00:07:07,058 --> 00:07:13,058
Idlewild is a crime, drama, music film directed by Bryan Barber.

2
00:14:14,117 --> 00:14:20,117
A reticent piano player Percival, along with Rooster, his flamboyant lead performer and manager, struggle to keep
their speakeasy, in the Prohibition-era South, out of the hands of gangsters who want to take it over.

3
00:21:21,176 --> 00:21:27,176
Percival, played by André 3000.

4
00:28:28,235 --> 00:28:34,235
Rooster, played by Big Boi.

5
00:35:35,294 --> 00:35:41,294
Angel, played by Paula Patton.

6
00:42:42,352 --> 00:42:48,352
Trumpy, played by Terrence Howard.

7
00:49:49,411 --> 00:49:55,411
Ace, played by Faizon Love.

8
00:56:56,470 --> 00:57:02,470
Zora, played by Malinda Williams.

9
01:04:03,529 --> 01:04:09,529
Idlewild is a 2006 American musical drama film
written and directed by Bryan Barber.

10
01:11:10,588 --> 01:11:16,588
The film stars André 3000 and Big Boi of the hip hop duo Outkast and features musical
numbers that were written, produced and chiefly performed by the group.

11
01:18:17,647 --> 01:18:23,647
Idlewild contrasts the group's hip-hop, funk, and soul sound against a story based on a juke joint
in the fictional town of Idlewild, during the Great Depression in Georgia in 1935.

12
01:25:24,705 --> 01:25:30,705
Distributed by Universal Pictures, the film is an HBO Films
co-production alongside Mosaic Media Group and Forensic Films.

13
01:32:31,764 --> 01:32:37,764
It features an ensemble cast including Terrence Howard, Paula Jai Parker, Paula Patton, Cicely Tyson, Ben Vereen, Patti
LaBelle, Ving Rhames, Macy Gray, Faizon Love, Bruce Bruce, Malinda Williams, Jackie Long and Bill Nunn.

14
01:39:38,823 --> 01:39:44,823
Idlewild received mixed reviews from critics and
grossed $12.6 million worldwide.

15
01:46:45,882 --> 01:46:51,882
The film explores themes of piano lessons, mortician,
tied to chair, song and dance, fisticuffs.

16
01:53:52,941 --> 01:53:58,941
The tone is emotional.
